From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 06:05:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rk3399-pinephone-pro: keep the 4G rails powered

0002 drops the quectel,eg25 node because LuneOS drives the modem from
userspace with eg25-manager. That node was also the only consumer of the
two modem supplies:

    power-supply = <&vcc_4g>;
    vbus-supply  = <&vcc_4g_5v>;

Both are plain regulator-fixed with an enable GPIO and no
regulator-always-on, so with the consumer gone the core never enables
them. On a running PinePhone Pro:

    /sys/kernel/debug/gpio
      gpio-23  (  |regulator-vcc-4g-5v ) out lo
      gpio-23  (  |regulator-vcc-4g    ) out lo

    /sys/kernel/debug/regulator/regulator_summary
      vcc_4g_5v   0  0   5000mV   0mA
      vcc_4g      0  0   3800mV   0mA

enable-active-high with the pin driven low means both rails are off, so
the EG25 has no power at all. eg25-manager then runs its power-on
sequence against a dead modem, nothing ever enumerates on USB, and ofono
comes up with no device:

    eg25-manager: Executed power-on sequence
    eg25-manager: Rescheduling upload since modem isn't online yet, in 30s
    ofonod: create_rilmodem: ofono_modem_register returned: -19

eg25-manager owns the modem's power sequencing through PWRKEY, RESET and
W_DISABLE#, not through these rails - it expects them to be present. Mark
them always-on so the supply is there for it to sequence.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS userspace policy]
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-pinephone-pro.dts | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-pinephone-pro.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-pinephone-pro.dts
@@ -427,6 +427,8 @@
 		gpio = <&gpio1 RK_PC7 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 		pinctrl-names = "default";
 		pinctrl-0 = <&vcc_4g_5v_en>;
+		regulator-always-on;
+		regulator-boot-on;
 		regulator-name = "vcc_4g_5v";
 		regulator-min-microvolt = <5000000>;
 		regulator-max-microvolt = <5000000>;
@@ -439,6 +441,8 @@
 		gpio = <&gpio4 RK_PC7 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 		pinctrl-names = "default";
 		pinctrl-0 = <&vcc_4g_en>;
+		regulator-always-on;
+		regulator-boot-on;
 		regulator-name = "vcc_4g";
 		regulator-min-microvolt = <3800000>;
 		regulator-max-microvolt = <3800000>;
